verses.text:
6:3And one cried to another, saying:
Holy, holy, holy is the Lord Sabaoth;
all the earth is full of His glory. [1] [2]

6:9And He said, Go, and say to this people:
Hearing, you will hear and certainly not understand;
and seeing, you will see and certainly not perceive.

7:15Curds and honey he will eat;
before he knows or chooses evil,
he will choose the good. [1]

9:1You people who walk in darkness, behold a great light;
you who dwell in a land and shadow of death,
a light will shine upon you. [1]

9:3For the yoke laid upon them has been taken away,
and the rod upon their neck;
for the Lord has shattered the rod of their oppressors,
as in the day against Midian.

9:4For every robe gathered by deceit,
and every garment, they will repay with restitution;
and they will wish that they had been burned with fire. [1]

11:3The spirit of the fear of God will fill him.
He will not judge according to appearance,
nor reprove according to report;

11:7And the ox and the bear will feed together,
and their young will be together;
and the lion and the ox will eat straw together. [1]

11:9And they will certainly do no harm,
nor will they be able at all to destroy anyone upon My holy mountain;
for the whole earth has been filled with the knowledge of the Lord,
as abundant water covers the seas.

40:2You priests, speak to the heart of Jerusalem; comfort her.
For her humiliation is fulfilled, her sin is loosed;
for from the hand of the Lord she has received double for her sins. [1]

40:3A voice of one crying in the wilderness:
Prepare the way of the Lord;
make straight the paths of our God. [1] [2]

40:5And the glory of the Lord will be seen,
and all flesh will see the salvation of God;
for the Lord has spoken.

40:11Like a shepherd, He will shepherd His flock;
and with His arm He will gather lambs,
and comfort those that are with young. [1]

53:6We all, like sheep, have gone astray;
each person has strayed in his own way.
And the Lord delivered him over to our sins. [1]

53:9And I will give the wicked in exchange for his burial,
and the rich in exchange for his death;
for he committed no iniquity,
nor was deceit found in his mouth. [1]

53:12Therefore he will inherit many,
and will divide the spoils of the mighty;
for his soul was delivered to death,
and he was numbered among the lawless.
And he bore the sins of many,
and for their sins he was delivered up. [1]

55:1You who thirst, go to the water;
and you who have no silver, go and buy wine and rich food,
and drink without silver or price. [1]

55:7let the ungodly forsake his ways,
and the lawless man his counsels;
and let him return to the Lord, and he will receive mercy;
for He will abundantly forgive your sins.

55:11so it will be with My word, whatever goes out from My mouth:
it will certainly not return until all that I have willed is accomplished;
and I will prosper your ways and My commandments. [1]

55:12For you will go out in gladness, and in joy you will be taught;
for the mountains and the hills will leap, welcoming you with joy,
and all the trees of the field will clap their branches. [1]
